; PhaseOrdering regression guard for extra-unroll-after-vectorize-passes:
; a 13x13 matmul kernel (trip count 13 is odd, prime, and small enough
; that the baseline's early LoopFullUnroll unrolls only the innermost
; k-reduction). The outer i-loop is deliberately kept as a real loop
; by the baseline because the combined i*j*k body would exceed the
; early full-unroll threshold.
;
; Baseline pipeline (opt.a):
;   early LoopFullUnrollPass fully unrolls only the innermost k-loop
;   (1 NumCompletelyUnrolled event); the i- and j-loops are left as
;   loops; SLP coalesces the inner body. Final IR has 2 loop
;   back-edges, 1 store, 93 instructions.
;
; With extra-unroll-after-vectorize-passes (opt.b):
;   the inner loops are deferred in the early pipeline; LV processes
;   the inner and the post-LV LoopFullUnrollPass then becomes able to
;   fully unroll the enclosing j- and i-loops too because the
;   LV-compacted body is smaller. Result: 14 NumCompletelyUnrolled
;   events (8-13x more than baseline), every output element materialised
;   as straight-line code, no i/j back-edges. Final IR has 1 back-edge
;   and 758 instructions (+716% over baseline). The regression is
;   visible all the way down to assembly: ~560 aarch64 instructions
;   with 182 fmul/fadd vs baseline's 62 / 26.
;
; This matches the dealii matrix_free and nektarpp MatrixFreeOps
; corpus regressions where files doubled or tripled in total
; instruction count exactly because of this chain of:
;   defer early unroll -> LV vectorize -> post-LV unroll everything.

